<<<<<<< HEAD
    "**Goal:** build one clean table with one row per loan, ready for the models. For each loan it holds the **target** (did it default within 24 months?) and the **features** (what was known when the loan started).\n",
    "\n",
    "**How this notebook relates to the script.** The final table is built by `src/build_modelling_table.py`, so that every notebook uses the same table. This notebook walks through each choice step by step, shows the evidence, and checks the result.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The one rule for features:** a feature may only use information that was known **when the loan started**. Anything that happens later (late payments, a modification, how the loan ended) would let the model see the future. That is called leakage, and it makes a model look far better than it really is."
